  "result": "NRS_484B_260 passes the gate with **OK** (6 witnesses), using 2 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n- **Run 1: `CHECK_FAIL`.** I had written \"the subject is ahead of v\" as a `rel_bearing` measure with a `\"longitudinal\"` component, but the measure only accepts `x`/`y`. I switched to the Boolean form `rel_bearing [v, subject, \"ahead\"]`, which means exactly what the record says: the bearing from v to the subject, in v's frame, points forward.\n- **Run 2: `OK`.**\n\n**Rule** (`NRS_484B_260.lean`):\n- **Subject:** a member of the vehicle aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the subject is moving faster than the halt tolerance and is in no alley. Its body overlaps a roadway r that lies on a highway h, and a driveway entrance e. It came onto e from off the roadway: it has stayed on e since an observation where it was on e and not on r.\n- **The duty:** for every such h, r and e (the full selection is written again in the obligation), it covers every other moving vehicle v that is on a travel region of h and has the subject ahead of it. The subject must not touch v. Their closest approach must also not come within `p.conflict_horizon` at a centre distance below `p.conflict_centre_clearance`.\n- **Narrowings:** none. Spelling \"ahead\" with the bearing atom was the only free choice, and it means exactly what the record states.\n\n**Witnesses** (`NRS_484B_260.lean` in the witness folder): three instants, 1 s apart. The subject heads north at 2 m/s out of a driveway entrance and straddles the entrance and the roadway at the last instant. Vehicle v drives east at 10 m/s in a lane on the same highway.\n\n| Scenario | Setup | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | v 20 m short of the crossing: closest approach ≈0.98 m after ≈1.98 s | violated |\n| permit | v 100 m short: closest approach ≈9.7 s out, past the horizon | compliant |\n| idle | subject drives along the roadway, never on the entrance | not applicable |\n| blind | forbid's trace with `st.on_way` masked | unknown |\n| branch_1 | forbid without v | compliant |\n| branch_2 | forbid, with the subject also on an alley | not applicable |\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- task_result.md",
